From: Sidharth Renukadevi <srenukad@qti.qualcomm.com>
Subject: [PATCH] QSDK:HOSTAPD: Guard station flush on uninitialized BSS

During hostapd reload, old BSS state is cleared before removing and
reinitializing an interface whose BSS/interface configuration changed.
Under MLO link/interface toggle stress, an AP link can already be in
HAPD_IFACE_UNINITIALIZED state while still holding a stale driver private
pointer. In that state, hostapd_flush_old_stations() calls into nl80211
and dereferences the stale i802_bss pointer, resulting in a crash in
nl80211_bss_msg().

Skip the driver station flush for an uninitialized BSS and clear the
stale drv_priv pointer so later cleanup does not reuse it.

Signed-off-by: Sidharth Renukadevi <srenukad@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/ap/hostapd.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/ap/hostapd.c b/src/ap/hostapd.c
index 6fddd7602ba4..111111111111 100644
--- a/src/ap/hostapd.c
+++ b/src/ap/hostapd.c
@@ -1345,6 +1345,14 @@ static int hostapd_flush_old_stations(struct hostapd_data *hapd, u16 reason)
 	if (hostapd_drv_none(hapd) || hapd->drv_priv == NULL)
 		return 0;
 
+	if (hapd->iface && hapd->iface->state == HAPD_IFACE_UNINITIALIZED) {
+		wpa_dbg(hapd->msg_ctx, MSG_DEBUG,
+			"Skip station flush on uninitialized BSS %s",
+			hapd->conf ? hapd->conf->iface : "N/A");
+		hapd->drv_priv = NULL;
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	if (!hapd->iface->driver_ap_teardown) {
 		wpa_dbg(hapd->msg_ctx, MSG_DEBUG,
 			"Flushing old station entries");
-- 

